<p>All six values are highly consistent. The maximum deviation is 0.4 percentage points (auto loan), which is obviously due to the standard rounding adopted by HowMuch in the editing process. No serious factual errors, ranking errors or data falsifications were found. Student loans (546%) and credit cards (19%) match exactly to the nearest integer.</p>


<h2>Part 6: Data Quality Examination</h2>
<p>The source of the data is the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, which is a highly credible and authoritative institution. The New York Federal Reserve compiles the Quarterly Report on Household Debt and Credit using data from Equifax Credit Reporting Agency. The data source uses rigorous, transparent and systematic methods for data collection and processing, and provides detailed documents, including detailed tables and method descriptions, to ensure that researchers and the public can obtain transparent and reliable information.</p>

<p><strong>Key limitations that audiences should be aware of:</strong></p>
<p>This is a summary of national data; regional differences and changes between individual households cannot be observed.</p>


